{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Python 3.12. Now I'll implement the fix in amap.py.\n\nDesign decisions:\n- Sliding window of at most `limit` tasks, items pulled lazily from `iter(items)` (support both sync and async iterables).\n- Index each item; store results by index; return in order.\n- Validate limit < 1 → ValueError before any work.\n- Fail-fast on error: cancel pending tasks, await cleanup, re-raise the error with lowest index in the completed batch (first observed batch).\n- finally cleanup handles caller cancellation.\n\nLet me write the file.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Python 3.12. Now I'll implement a sliding-window version in `amap.py`: it pulls items lazily so at most `limit` tasks exist at once, tags each item with its index so results can be reassembled in input order regardless of completion order, supports sync and async iterables, and fails fast (cancelling siblings) on errors."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00004]","name":"write_file","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/flashbench_deepseek_v41/t07/amap.py","content":"import asyncio\n\n\nasync def bounded_map(fn, items, limit):\n    if limit < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"limit must be at least 1\")\n\n    if hasattr(items, \"__aiter__\"):\n        aiterator = items.__aiter__()\n\n        async def pull():\n            try:\n                return True, await aiterator.__anext__()\n            except StopAsyncIteration:\n                return False, None\n    else:\n        iterator = iter(items)\n\n        async def pull():\n            try:\n                return True, next(iterator)\n            except StopIteration:\n                return False, None\n\n    pending = {}\n    results = {}\n    submitted = 0\n    exhausted = False\n\n    async def fill():\n        nonlocal submitted, exhausted\n        while not exhausted and len(pending) < limit:\n            more, item = await pull()\n            if not more:\n                exhausted = True\n                return\n            task = asyncio.ensure_future(fn(item))\n            pending[task] = submitted\n            submitted += 1\n\n    await fill()\n    try:\n        while pending:\n            done, _ = await asyncio.wait(\n                list(pending), return_when=asyncio.FIRST_COMPLETED\n            )\n            error = None\n            for task in done:\n                index = pending.pop(task)\n                exc = task.exception()\n                if exc is not None:\n                    if error is None or index < error[0]:\n                        error = (index, exc)\n                else:\n                    results[index] = task.result()\n            if error is not None:\n                raise error[1]\n            await fill()\n    finally:\n        if pending:\n            for task in pending:\n                task.cancel()\n            await asyncio.gather(*pending, return_exceptions=True)\n\n    return [results[index] for index in range(submitted)]\n"}}]}}
