{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file is correct now: initial fill inside the try. Let me now run all tests again including a new test for iterator-raises-mid-iteration cleanup, then run the public test and comprehensive suite.\n\nNew test: generator that yields some items then raises; verify pending child tasks are cancelled/cleaned within an existing loop.\n\n```python\nasync def main():\n    async def slow(x):\n        try:\n            await asyncio.sleep(30)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            raise\n        return x\n    def gen():\n        yield 1\n        yield 2\n        raise RuntimeError(\"iterator failed\")\n    try:\n        await bounded_map(slow, gen(), 5)\n    except RuntimeError:\n        pass\n    await asyncio.sleep(0)\n    return [t for t in asyncio.all_tasks() if t is not asyncio.current_task()]\nassert asyncio.run(main()) == []\n```\n\nWait — in this scenario, fill pulls items 1 and 2, creating tasks, then pulls → generator raises RuntimeError. Exception propagates from fill inside try → finally cancels tasks 1,2 → gathers them. Then RuntimeError propagates. Good.\n\nAlso test async iterator raising mid-iteration.\n\nLet me re-run the whole suite with these additions.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"File is correct. Now re-running the full suite plus a new case where the iterable itself raises mid-iteration."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00015]","name":"shell_command","input":{"command":"python3 -W error::DeprecationWarning -W error::RuntimeWarning test_public.py && python3 -W error::DeprecationWarning -W error::RuntimeWarning - <<'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nfrom amap import bounded_map\n\nasync def ident(x): return x\nasync def double(x): return x * 2\n\ndef run_probe(items, limit, delays):\n    state = {\"active\": 0, \"max\": 0, \"calls\": 0}\n    async def fn(x):\n        state[\"active\"] += 1\n        state[\"max\"] = max(state[\"max\"], state[\"active\"])\n        state[\"calls\"] += 1\n        try:\n            await asyncio.sleep(delays[x % len(delays)])\n            return x * 10\n        finally:\n            state[\"active\"] -= 1\n    out = asyncio.run(bounded_map(fn, items, limit))\n    return out, state\nout, st = run_probe(list(range(200)), 8, [0.003, 0.0, 0.001, 0.002])\nassert out == [i * 10 for i in range(200)] and st[\"max\"] == 8 and st[\"calls\"] == 200, st\nout, st = run_probe(list(range(10)), 1, [0.0005])\nassert out == [i * 10 for i in range(10)] and st[\"max\"] == 1, st\n\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(double, (1, 2, 3), 2)) == [2, 4, 6]\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(double, range(5), 3)) == [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]\ns = {1, 2, 3}\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(double, s, 2)) == [x * 2 for x in s]\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(ident, {\"a\": 1}, 1)) == [\"a\"]\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(ident, (i for i in range(6)), 2)) == list(range(6))\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(ident, [], 3)) == []\nasync def agen():\n    for i in range(5): yield i\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(ident, agen(), 2)) == list(range(5))\n\nlim_state = {\"active\": 0, \"max\": 0}\nasync def frac(x):\n    lim_state[\"active\"] += 1\n    lim_state[\"max\"] = max(lim_state[\"max\"], lim_state[\"active\"])\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.001)\n    lim_state[\"active\"] -= 1\n    return x\nassert asyncio.run(bounded_map(frac, range(20), 2.5)) == list(range(20))\nassert lim_state[\"max\"] <= 2.5, lim_state\n\nfor bad in (0, -1, -7, 0.5):\n    try:\n        asyncio.run(bounded_map(ident, [1, 2, 3], bad))\n    except ValueError:\n        pass\n    else:\n        raise AssertionError(f\"expected ValueError for limit={bad}\")\n\n# iterator raising mid-iteration must clean up already-started tasks\nasync def main_iter_err():\n    async def slow(x):\n        try:\n            await asyncio.sleep(30)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            raise\n        return x\n\n    def gen():\n        yield 1\n        yield 2\n        raise RuntimeError(\"iterator failed\")\n\n    try:\n        await bounded_map(slow, gen(), 5)\n    except RuntimeError:\n        pass\n    else:\n        raise AssertionError(\"expected RuntimeError\")\n    await asyncio.sleep(0)\n    return [t for t in asyncio.all_tasks() if t is not asyncio.current_task()]\nassert asyncio.run(main_iter_err()) == []\n\n# async iterator raising mid-iteration\nasync def main_aiter_err():\n    async def slow(x):\n        try:\n            await asyncio.sleep(30)\n        except asyncio.CancelledError:\n            raise\n        return x\n\n    async def agen_bad():\n        yield 1\n        yield 2\n        raise RuntimeError(\"aiterator failed\")\n\n    try:\n        await bounded_map(slow, agen_bad(), 5)\n    except RuntimeError:\n        pass\n    else:\n        raise AssertionError(\"expected RuntimeError\")\n    await asyncio.sleep(0)\n    return [t for t in asyncio.all_tasks() if t is not asyncio.current_task()]\nassert asyncio.run(main_aiter_err()) == []\n\n# laziness invariant\nlimit = 4\nstate = {\"pulls\": 0, \"completed\": 0, \"violations\": 0}\ndef gen2():\n    i = 0\n    while i < 300:\n        state[\"pulls\"] += 1\n        yield i\n        i += 1\nasync def lazy(x):\n    if state[\"pulls\"] - state[\"completed\"] > limit:\n        state[\"violations\"] += 1\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.0005)\n    state[\"completed\"] += 1\n    return x\nout = asyncio.run(bounded_map(lazy, gen2(), limit))\nassert out == list(range(300)) and state[\"violations\"] == 0, state\n\nclass Boom(Exception): pass\ninf_state = {\"pulls\": 0, \"created\": 0}\ndef inf_gen():\n    i = 0\n    while True:\n        inf_state[\"pulls\"] += 1\n        yield i\n        i += 1\nasync def fail_on_10(x):\n    inf_state[\"created\"] += 1\n    if x == 10: raise Boom(\"stop\")\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.0005)\n    return x\ntry:\n    asyncio.run(bounded_map(fail_on_10, inf_gen(), 3))\nexcept Boom:\n    pass\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError(\"expected Boom\")\nassert inf_state[\"pulls\"] <= inf_state[\"created\"] + 3, inf_state\n\nctx_errors = []\nloop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\nloop.set_exception_handler(lambda lp, ctx: ctx_errors.append(ctx))\nasyncio.set_event_loop(loop)\nclass Fail3(Exception): pass\nasync def boom3(x):\n    if x == 3: raise Fail3(\"x=3\")\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.005)\n    return x\nasync def main_fail():\n    try:\n        await bounded_map(boom3, range(50), 4)\n    except Fail3:\n        pass\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.01)\n    return [t for t in asyncio.all_tasks() if t is not asyncio.current_task()]\nleftover = loop.run_until_complete(main_fail())\nloop.run_until_complete(asyncio.sleep(0.02))\nloop.close()\nasyncio.set_event_loop(None)\nassert leftover == [] and ctx_errors == [], (leftover, ctx_errors)\n\ncstate = {\"started\": 0, \"cancelled\": 0}\nasync def hang(x):\n    cstate[\"started\"] += 1\n    try:\n        await asyncio.sleep(30)\n    except asyncio.CancelledError:\n        cstate[\"cancelled\"] += 1\n        raise\n    return x\nasync def main_cancel():\n    t = asyncio.ensure_future(bounded_map(hang, range(50), 3))\n    await asyncio.sleep(0.05)\n    t.cancel()\n    try:\n        await t\n    except asyncio.CancelledError:\n        pass\n    await asyncio.sleep(0)\n    return [x for x in asyncio.all_tasks() if x is not asyncio.current_task()]\nleft = asyncio.run(main_cancel())\nassert cstate == {\"started\": 3, \"cancelled\": 3}, cstate\nassert left == [], left\n\nprint(\"ALL CHECKS PASSED\")\nEOF","description":"Full suite including iterator-failure cleanup","cwd":"/tmp/flashbench_deepseek_v41/t07"}}]}}
